e-1lwbk6pl0.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Methoxy group is o-, p-directing. Nitration of methoxy benzene will produce p-isomer as the major product due to steric crowding in o-isomers. Bromination of p-nitroanisole (A) with excess of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.476ex\" height=\"1.885ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1536.6 833\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use><use data-c=\"72\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-72\" transform=\"translate(708,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1133,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> will result in disubstitution to give 2, 5-dibromo-4-nitroanisole.\n(B) as the major product.</p>"}]}